     canonical  marginalised per-cluster p = NGC 2419 6.98e-02, Pal 3 3.70e-01, Pal 4 2.15e-05, Pal 14 2.77e-03  |  Fisher-combined 2.49e-06 (4.6 sigma)
     alt        marginalised per-cluster p = NGC 2419 4.54e-02, Pal 3 2.92e-01, Pal 4 1.02e-05, Pal 14 1.74e-03  |  Fisher-combined 4.91e-07 (4.9 sigma)

  AGAINST MY OWN STATISTIC, and this is the most important caveat in the script: at Gentile+2010's own numbers (sigma_MOND = 1.27 km/s, Jordi+2009's 0.38 km/s from 16 stars) the chi^2 dispersion statistic used here gives p = 2.0e-06, while THEIR Kolmogorov-Smirnov test on the same data gave p = 0.27-0.36 (64-73% confidence).  The gap is the STATISTIC, not the data: chi^2 on the dispersion is the sufficient statistic for a Gaussian width and is far more powerful than a KS test on the full CDF with a floating centre.  That makes the numbers here much stronger than the published ones -- and it also makes them much more fragile, because chi^2 assumes clean membership and Gaussianity, where one mis-assigned star or one unmodelled binary moves sigma_hat directly.  The two are not comparable and neither is quoted as the other.
  what a uniform error in the measured dispersions would do (the adversarial direction -- if every measured sigma here is too LOW, the framework is rescued):
     every measured sigma x1.00 -> marginalised Fisher-combined p = 2.49e-06 (4.6 sigma)
     every measured sigma x1.15 -> marginalised Fisher-combined p = 2.89e-04 (3.4 sigma)
     every measured sigma x1.30 -> marginalised Fisher-combined p = 6.20e-03 (2.5 sigma)
     every measured sigma x1.50 -> marginalised Fisher-combined p = 7.25e-02 (1.5 sigma)
  [PASS] 93h the combined exclusion survives marginalising over a realistic stellar-M/L prior, but it drops by two orders of magnitude when it does; a uniform 30% underestimate of the measured dispersions would take it to 2.5 sigma and a 50% one to 1.5 sigma.  That is the honest size of the result: a bound on the outer-halo globulars' stellar M/L, quoted as the marginalised number, never as the fixed-M/L one   (canonical: fixed-M/L p = 2.74e-08, marginalised p = 2.49e-06 (4.6 sigma); alt marginalised p = 4.91e-07; marginalised p if every measured sigma is 30% too low = 6.20e-03)

