NGC 2419's dispersion profile -- the shape test (Ibata et al. 2011), done with the raw bins and nothing else
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  the measured profile falls as sigma ~ R^(-0.713 +- 0.091) over 16-92 pc (0.8-4.6 half-light radii)
  Keplerian (all mass inside, Newtonian, isotropic) is -0.500; isolated deep-MOND is 0.000.  The measurement is 2.3 sigma STEEPER than Keplerian.
  [PASS] 93i NGC 2419's outer dispersion profile declines FASTER than Keplerian, where the framework needs it to decline SLOWER -- but this script declines to call that a kill, because line-of-sight projection, radial anisotropy and tidal truncation all steepen an observed sigma(R) in Newtonian gravity too, and separating them needs the full dynamical models Ibata+2011 and Sanders 2012 disagreed about.  Recorded as a consistent SIGN, not a measurement   (measured slope -0.713 +- 0.091 (2.3 sigma steeper than Keplerian); NGC 2419 is also the cluster with all the statistical weight (183 radial velocities) and the SMALLEST boost (1.28x, y_int/y_ext = 89) -- the power and the lever are in different clusters)

